  "text": "Recipe: Corn Oats Crackers\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Crackers\nIngredients: 1/2 cup corn flour (chakki atta), 1/2 cup residue of oat milk, 1 cup mixed vegetables (minced fine), red onion, sponge gourd, grated carrot, amla berries, plantain, raw papaya, other veggies of your choice, a small piece of ginger, 1/2 green chili, a few curry leaves, 1/2 tsp turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp roasted cumin seeds powder, 1/4 tsp carom seeds, 1/4 tsp hing (asafoetada), 1/4 tsp black pepper, 1/4 tsp garlic powder, 1/4 tsp mustard powder, sesame seeds, pumpkin seeds, rolled oats\nCooking methods: bake\nInstructions: Mix all the ingredients into a firm dough; adjust flour and veggies as necessary.\nMake small balls with the batter. Give them shapes of your choice. Sprinkle sesame seeds, or pumpkin seeds or rolled oats on top.\nPlace them in a baking pan lined with parchment paper. Bake both sides for 20 and 10 minutes, respectively, at 180 C.",
